QEMU Cocoa: make a console's GL texture when it is first drawn

What: cocoa_gl_switch and the extra displays' omacvm_head_gfx_switch drop
the old surface's texture and make none for the new one. It is made whole
(glTexImage2D of the surface; the surface holds the whole picture) on
QEMU's thread when something draws it: at the surface's first update (2D:
the firmware, the boot console), at a present without a GL scanout, or at
the refresh tick before a CAOpenGLLayer (GPU safe mode, extra displays)
draws it. Readers on the AppKit thread draw black until it is there and
never make it. The boot logo stands in for the "display not active"
placeholder, so with the logo on (the default) the placeholder gets no
texture at all. OMACVM_CONSOLE_TEXTURE=eager makes it at every switch, as
before. qemu.log once: "cocoa: console texture: made when first drawn" or
"... made at every switch (OMACVM_CONSOLE_TEXTURE=eager)". Test hook:
OMACVM_TEST_CONSOLE_CHECK=1 reads every frame drawn from the console
texture (the present and the CAOpenGLLayer path) back at 8 x 8 points and
compares them with the surface ("cocoa: console check (PATH): ..."); the
present's surfaces stay plain then.
Why: with virgl the window shows the guest's scanout texture and never the
console texture, yet every set scanout made one: qemu_console_resize at
each mode change and display on, the placeholder at each display off (at
the old size), each upload under the BQL. Apple's GL keeps a second copy
of a texture filled from client memory: 127.4 MiB of QEMU's footprint per
5120x2880 output (host test without a VM, vm-memory host-code gfxmem:
console 127.4 vs console-nodata 0). #609's rows: up to 218.6 ms of BQL
per upload, 161-170 holds of 20 ms or more in 60 display off/on cycles.
Upstream: the console texture code is upstream's (ui/console-gl.c); the
callers are OmacVM's texture-borrowing and heads patches. Not sent.
Tests: Tests/display/test-console-texture.sh (build time: the listeners
and console-gl.c's helpers from the patched files with a GL stub that
counts uploaded bytes: a GL scanout and 3 display off/on cycles upload
nothing (3.2.16: 5120x2880x4 at every switch), the placeholder without
the logo one 640x480 upload, a 2D surface one whole upload at its first
update; the readers' wiring; --self-test: all fail on the code before).
